{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.HeckeMassTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.HeckeMassTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Group.Basic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Arch.mass_markov_archimedean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Arch.mass_markov_archimedean","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L157-L173","doc":"Compatibility with the archimedean mass formula:\n|tr_M(Φ_mass)| = Vol(K) / ℏ_q² when the Markov trace evaluates\nto the hyperbolic volume divided by the quantum Planck constant\nsquared.\n\nThis is the Kashaev/dilogarithm bridge: it explicitly applies\nthe fibre functor τ and so lives strictly in the Archimedean\ntier (`conj:phi-q-tower-jsj-bridge`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Arch.mass_markov_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Arch.mass_markov_exact","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L139-L155","doc":"Exact decomposition when both trace components are non-negative\n(as guaranteed in the archimedean realisation, where trace values\nare norms of holonomies and quantum dilogarithms). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Arch.mass_markov_upper_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Arch.mass_markov_upper_bound","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L130-L137","doc":"The mass decomposes via the triangle inequality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Arch.categoricalMassFromMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Arch.categoricalMassFromMarkov","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L110-L128","doc":"**Mass via the Markov trace** (Proposition):\n\nThe categorical mass equals the absolute value of the Markov trace\nof the Hecke mass element:\n\n  m(ϱ_β) = |tr_M(Φ_mass(β))|\n\nThis follows from:\n1. The fibre functor τ is exact and monoidal\n2. τ sends the categorical trace to the Markov trace (Jones)\n3. τ sends the mass integrand to the Hecke mass element (Schur–Weyl)\n4. The norm over ℝ is the absolute value ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Arch.MarkovMassData.trace_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Arch.MarkovMassData.trace_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L108-L108","doc":"Linearity of tr_M: tr_M(Φ_mass) = tr_M(Φ^desc) + tr_M(Φ^trans). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Arch.MarkovMassData.transientTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Arch.MarkovMassData.transientTrace","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L106-L106","doc":"The Markov trace of the transient component: tr_M(Φ^trans). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Arch.MarkovMassData.descendedTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Arch.MarkovMassData.descendedTrace","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L104-L104","doc":"The Markov trace of the descended component: tr_M(Φ^desc). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Arch.MarkovMassData.markovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Arch.MarkovMassData.markovTrace","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L102-L102","doc":"The Markov trace of the mass element: tr_M(Φ_mass(β)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Arch.MarkovMassData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Arch.MarkovMassData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Arch.MarkovMassData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Arch.MarkovMassData","kind":"structure","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L88-L108","doc":"Data for the Markov trace computation of mass.\n\nEncodes the fibre-functor image: the categorical trace becomes\nthe Markov trace, and the mass integrand becomes the Hecke mass\nelement.  The norm of tr_M(Φ_mass) equals the categorical mass.\n\nPer `QOU.GroundRingAnnotations`, this is the Archimedean\nrealisation; the pre-Arch declaration lives in `Pre` above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Pre.categoricalMassSquaredFromMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Pre.categoricalMassSquaredFromMarkov","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L69-L78","doc":"**Pre-Arch mass via the Markov trace.**\n\nThe categorical mass-squared equals the Frobenius pairing of\n`tr_M(Φ_mass)` with itself, valued in `R`.  Caller supplies\nthe Frobenius pairing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Pre.MarkovMassData.trace_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Pre.MarkovMassData.trace_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Linearity of `tr_M`:\n`tr_M(Φ_mass) = tr_M(Φ^desc) + tr_M(Φ^trans)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Pre.MarkovMassData.transientTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Pre.MarkovMassData.transientTrace","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The Markov trace of the transient component: `tr_M(Φ^trans)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Pre.MarkovMassData.descendedTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Pre.MarkovMassData.descendedTrace","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The Markov trace of the descended component: `tr_M(Φ^desc)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Pre.MarkovMassData.markovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Pre.MarkovMassData.markovTrace","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The Markov trace of the mass element: `tr_M(Φ_mass(β))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Pre.MarkovMassData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Pre.MarkovMassData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.Pre.MarkovMassData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.Pre.MarkovMassData","kind":"structure","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-trace.lean#L46-L67","doc":"Pre-Arch data for the Markov trace computation of mass.\n\nPolymorphic in the ground field `R`.  Encodes the fibre-functor\nimage: the categorical trace becomes the Markov trace, and the\nmass integrand becomes the Hecke mass element.  The Frobenius\nnorm of `tr_M(Φ_mass)` (computed in `R`, not `ℝ`) equals the\ncategorical mass. ","signatureChunk":0}]}